ound, and reverse flow roles"}, {"id": "a8723a45-21ae-4476-9076-980fad40cf9a", "type": "concept", "title": "Customer promise, lead time, and geographic coverage"}], "description": "Students learn why warehouses exist and how their role changes across distribution networks."}, {"id": "906f39c5-f404-4f39-bf8b-0efa31004101", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Operating model choices", "children": [{"id": "05ab356f-dcef-44d1-a6a9-7e11b0abc68c", "type": "concept", "title": "Service-level targets"}, {"id": "96ed4778-348a-4e8e-9bbe-f7c88dd41490", "type": "concept", "title": "Process standardization"}, {"id": "cb72751b-57d7-4e75-98d3-0ac14944b56c", "type": "concept", "title": "Automation readiness"}, {"id": "df0c849c-7ed8-4200-abf7-3b68f7da7209", "type": "concept", "title": "Governance and continuous improvement"}], "description": "This subtopic connects policy, process, technology, and labor into one operating system."}]}, {"id": "3fd8d715-cad1-49fa-9a65-42ad74d526d8", "type": "topic", "title": "Inventory Costs, Tradeoffs, and Financial Impact", "description": "Analyze carrying, ordering, shortage, obsolescence, and working-capital costs.", "children": [{"id": "3a205423-28ab-4384-ba08-0c4edebdfb06", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Inventory cost categories", "children": [{"id": "1bffe2c0-5af8-4a07-b290-7ce96d718e96", "type": "concept", "title": "Carrying cost, ordering cost, shortage cost, obsolescence, damage, shrinkage, and handling cost"}, {"id": "2ba82890-1a71-4707-849b-4e7e124c7920", "type": "concept", "title": "Capital cost and opportunity cost"}, {"id": "83fa0ee8-3c6a-45f9-81e2-597bb9b3f588", "type": "concept", "title": "Storage, insurance, taxes, and depreciation"}, {"id": "35805cb9-48b6-4a5c-931c-5e9f6d19a10c", "type": "concept", "title": "Cost-to-serve by item or customer"}], "description": "Students learn to identify the true cost of inventory decisions beyond unit price."}, {"id": "54055882-1943-4c07-b680-4cac349425f5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Financial statemen