 "Promotions, launches, and end-of-life effects"}, {"id": "178326f1-d748-4520-9dc8-f2baf7750f14", "type": "concept", "title": "Demand sensing and exception signals"}], "description": "Inventory policies depend on how demand behaves. Students learn to distinguish stable, seasonal, intermittent, promotional, and lumpy demand."}, {"id": "826ba3b7-11ae-49e2-9952-974db38f044c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Forecasting inputs", "children": [{"id": "cea951e8-14cd-4d36-90c2-2166beb631bd", "type": "concept", "title": "Historical demand, orders, shipments, lost sales, and substitutions"}, {"id": "f915ecd0-3516-40c8-bd14-ea96e56d9a54", "type": "concept", "title": "Lead times, supplier reliability, and minimum order quantities"}, {"id": "0bb65f48-eb20-41bb-850d-96c6814e6e1c", "type": "concept", "title": "Forecast error and bias"}, {"id": "53996d95-9023-4403-9f83-e465608639ca", "type": "concept", "title": "Collaborative inputs from sales, procurement, and operations"}], "description": "This subtopic teaches students what data planners need before calculating inventory targets."}, {"id": "41c085e1-3cf6-4b09-99aa-8198e7e585fb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Replenishment logic", "children": [{"id": "55c5b825-2e80-4690-92ce-e4ceabd5136a", "type": "concept", "title": "Continuous review versus periodic review"}, {"id": "5371314c-6e5d-45a7-944b-0388b4bd932b", "type": "concept", "title": "Min-max systems"}, {"id": "a06de685-940b-49da-b573-e6375aca361d", "type": "concept", "title": "Order-up-to levels"}, {"id": "725a41ea-3339-4609-86e6-cc4b8b2bf4a8", "type": "concept", "title": "Planning calendars and review frequency"}], "description": "Students learn how forecast, demand history, lead time, and service targets translate into ordering decisions."}]}, {"id": "05177dc0-51d6-452d-bd2f-4a8a7ef4fe98", "type": "topic", "title": "EOQ, Reorder Points, and Lot-Sizing Models", "description": "Use foundational inventory models to set order quantities and replenishment triggers.", "children": [{"